{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:045c5a6050db60fe","name":"Antivehicle Mine","source":{"id":"source:reference-045c5a6050db60fe","title":"Antivehicle Mine","revision":15858,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:53:20Z","sha256":"7c181f557961729ea5599f4a9d23b54c72f5a51401f33c5f54126239dfa944ce","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15858","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Antivehicle%20Mine&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-045c5a6050db60fe","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 1,500\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 0.5 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mines, unlike traditional ",{"tag":"a","children":["Explosives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Explosives"},", are designed to be placed in the ground or otherwise hidden from sight. Anyone attempting to notice a Mine takes a -5 penalty on his or her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check. Setting a Mine is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"}," that does not require a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check. However, attaching a detonator (either a Timer or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Manual Trigger"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Manual_Trigger","referenceId":"reference:3bac33a88449a688"},") requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check as usual, and supersedes the Mine's normal triggering system.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Antivehicle Mine was designed specifically to damage many types of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},". An Antivehicle Mine is placed on the ground (in any square adjacent to you) and is triggered when any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ground Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ground_Vehicle"}," enters the square in which it is placed. An Antivehicle Mine cannot be triggered by anything other than a Vehicle moving through its square, ensuring that it is not accidentally triggered by a trooper and maximizing the damage to enemy ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},".  An Antivehicle Mine damages everything in a 2-square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"}," radius.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size:"]}," Diminutive\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 10d6 (Energy)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Radius:"]}," 2-Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"},")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
